# kin/youth/legs/far: the FAR leg of the youth side walk and run, a whole leg on its own part (KIN-YOUTH, P2b motion
# rollout, 2026-10-22; docs/MOTION_P2.md 7 and 12). The legs layer draws this part first (z -1) and kin/youth/legs/std (the
# near leg, z 0) over it, so the far leg is drawn full width (the youth idle's 4 px leg, the same capsule as the near
# leg) and only the pixels the near leg covers are hidden. Its value: the youth idle's far leg (cloth 2, leather h then g:
# the first interior pixel of each row lit), never one flat dark; the boot is the library's far key (boots_youth Y*f).
# Side views only (R, L) of the walk and run keys; the front and back views of the shared keys are empty (std draws both
# legs there). Written with std by the KIN-YOUTH leg kit from per-frame joint runs, then checked by eye at 8x; the L
# views are the R pixels mirrored and re-lit for the top-left light. Boy and girl share it.
use person
body youth
role legs std
layer legs
z -1
anchor pivot
keys legs
stamps boots_youth
tags boots-stamped

